   "source": [
    "rel = pd.DataFrame({c: stats.spearmanr(df[c], df[TARGET], nan_policy=\"omit\")[:2] for c in num}, index=[\"rho\", \"p\"]).T\n",
    "if len(rel):\n",
    "    rel[\"abs\"] = rel[\"rho\"].abs(); rel = rel.sort_values(\"abs\", ascending=False)\n",
    "    r_crit = np.tanh(1.96 / np.sqrt(len(df) - 3))\n",
    "    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, max(4, .25*len(rel))))\n",
    "    rel[\"rho\"].iloc[::-1].plot.barh(ax=ax, color=np.where(rel[\"rho\"].iloc[::-1] > 0, \"#2a7f8f\", \"#c9a227\"))\n",
    "    ax.axvline(r_crit, ls=\"--\", c=\"gray\"); ax.axvline(-r_crit, ls=\"--\", c=\"gray\")\n",
    "    ax.set_title(f\"Spearman feature vs ln(TDPA) (líneas: |rho| crítico={r_crit:.2f})\"); savefig(\"08_corr_with_target\")\n",
    "    display(rel.round(3).head(20))\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"Asociación feature–objetivo pendiente hasta calcular features territoriales para los TOP.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "96f78035",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "> **Advertencia de leakage:** este ranking es descriptivo. Si se usa para *seleccionar* features, la selección debe\n",
    "> repetirse dentro de cada fold de entrenamiento; seleccionar con todos los datos y luego validar infla las métricas."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
